    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.HelpTitle">How do I get a Client ID?</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step1">1. Open Google Cloud Console (console.cloud.google.com) and create a new project.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step2">2. In "APIs &amp; Services" → "Library", enable the Google Calendar API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step3">3. Configure the OAuth consent screen: type "External", and add your Gmail address under "Test users".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step4">4. Go to "Credentials" → "Create credentials" → "OAuth client ID".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step5">5. Choose "Desktop app" as the application type and click "Create".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Calendar.Google.Step6">6. Copy the Client ID and Client secret into the fields above, then click "Connect Google".</sys:String>
