    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Mods.GuideTitle">Quick guide</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Mods.Guide1">1. Create a sub folder in the mods folder, e.g. mods\my-widget.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Mods.Guide2">2. Widget: mod.json (id, name, kind: "widget", tab / tile, data: url or command) + view.xaml with {Binding Data.path} bindings.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Mods.Guide3">3. C# mod: a class library with a public INotchMod class (AddTab, AddTile, ShowHud) + mod.json with kind: "assembly" and the DLL name.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Mods.Guide4">4. Restart NotchHub - the mod shows up in this list and its tab after the built-in tabs.</sys:String>
