    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.HelpTitle">How to get a Client ID (5 steps)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Step1">1. Open developer.spotify.com/dashboard and sign in with your Spotify account.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Step2">2. Click "Create app" and enter any name and description (e.g. NotchHub).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Step3">3. Under "Redirect URIs" add exactly: http://127.0.0.1:43819/callback (not "localhost") and click "Add".</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Step4">4. Under "Which API/SDKs are you planning to use?" tick "Web API", accept the terms and save.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Step5">5. In the app settings copy the "Client ID", paste it above and click "Connect to Spotify". No Client Secret is needed (PKCE).</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Notes">Notes: development-mode apps require the owner to have Premium and only work for accounts added under "User Management". Controlling shuffle and repeat through the API requires Premium. Smart Shuffle is not available in Spotify's public API.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.OpenDashboard">Open Spotify for Developers</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Denied">Access was denied in the browser.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Expired">The Spotify session expired or was revoked - connect again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Client">Spotify does not recognise this Client ID - check that it was copied correctly.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Timeout">No answer from the browser. Make sure the Spotify dashboard lists exactly the redirect URI {0}.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Cancelled">Sign-in was cancelled.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Port">Port 43819 is used by another program - close it and try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Network">Can't reach Spotify - check your internet connection.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Premium">This feature (shuffle / repeat through the API) requires Spotify Premium.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.User">Spotify rejected the account - add it under "User Management" of your app in the developer dashboard.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.RateLimited">Too many requests to Spotify - try again in a moment.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Flow">Sign-in failed - please try again.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="settings.Spotify.Err.Other">Spotify error: {0}</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
